"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tprodCoeff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv_lhs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCon</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lift_coe</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⨂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₛₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⨂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mapAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">map_add'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map_add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">map_smul'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induction_on</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tprodCoeff_eq_smul_tprod</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smul_tprodCoeff'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mapAux_tprodCoeff</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map_tprod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tprod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tprod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">tprod_eq_tprodCoeff_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mapAux_tprodCoeff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Relate to lift of `MultilinearMap` (previous definition) when R₁ = R₂ and σ = id</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map_eq_lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">PiTensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tprod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compLinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614824337,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1785953029
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This would be enough for my original purpose, but perhaps this is a good opportunity to generalize further. I'm not sure I understand what the correct statement would be with a family of homomorphisms: would it still be of the following shape?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₛₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⨂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₛₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">??</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⨂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614824475,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1785953061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My comment about families of homomorphisms was for <code>MultilinearMap</code></p>",
        "id": 614829534,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785954650
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the type of your <code>map</code> is fine as is</p>",
        "id": 614829642,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785954687
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1017284\">Gregory Loges</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Inner.20product.20for.20PiTensorProduct/near/614824337\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks everyone, I was able to refactor <code>PiTensorProduct.map</code> with fixed rings and fixed ring homomorphism:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think you should instead first work on a generalization of <code>MultilinearMap</code> to the semilinear case.</p>",
        "id": 614832096,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1785955469
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Inner.20product.20for.20PiTensorProduct/near/614594488\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would we want a family of rings / ring homomorphisms for the semilinear case, or would one suffice?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I would be tempted to just use a single ring homomorphism, but maybe this is just asking for another refactor down the line. I'm worried that doing the typeclass inference on the pi-type everywhere would cause headaches; this may be worrying over nothing though.</p>",
        "id": 614832449,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1785955593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One place where the need for a family becomes plausible is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MultilinearMap.compLinearMap#doc\">docs#MultilinearMap.compLinearMap</a>, where if every module can be different, presumably we also want the rings to be able to change</p>",
        "id": 614833124,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785955830
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But I think it would be very reasonable to initially fix the morphism, and revisit when we have a compelling need for the family</p>",
        "id": 614833179,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785955849
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>An example for when families of ring homomorphisms are useful is sesquilinear forms: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=inner%E2%82%9B%E2%82%97#doc\">docs#innerₛₗ</a> is linear in one, and conjugate-linear in the other argument. That's why in my previous attempt, I fixed the rings but allowed an indexed family of ring homomorphisms. That way you don't have to deal with typeclass inferences over pi-types but still have enough flexibility for expressing sesquilinear forms.</p>",
        "id": 614835370,
        "sender_full_name": "Justus Springer",
        "timestamp": 1785956634
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've pushed my old attempt of making multi-semilinear maps to <a href=\"https://github.com/justus-springer/mathlib4/tree/justus/multisemilinear\">a branch of my fork</a>, if anyone wants to take a look. I did this in one afternoon and then never had motivation to continue. Feel free to take anything from there if it seems useful.</p>",
        "id": 614835903,
        "sender_full_name": "Justus Springer",
        "timestamp": 1785956816
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But also feel free to ignore it and do it differently :)</p>",
        "id": 614836005,
        "sender_full_name": "Justus Springer",
        "timestamp": 1785956853
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>wouldn't that need to be reflected in the tensor product itself?</p>",
        "id": 614836778,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785957156
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>I've pushed my old attempt of making multi-semilinear maps to <a href=\"https://github.com/justus-springer/mathlib4/tree/justus/multisemilinear\">a branch of my fork</a>, if anyone wants to take a look. I did this in one afternoon and then never had motivation to continue. Feel free to take anything from there if it seems useful.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thanks for sharing <span aria-label=\"slight smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f642\" role=\"img\" title=\"slight smile\">:slight_smile:</span><br>\nI'm on board to try taking a stab at generalizing <code>MultilinearMap</code> and then <code>PiTensorProduct.lift</code>, that way <code>PiTensorProduct.map</code> can be left unchanged.<br>\nIt looks like both <code>ContinuousMultilinearMap</code> and <code>AlternatingMap</code> depend on <code>MultilinearMap</code> so perhaps sticking with a fixed ring homomorphism to start will minimize the ripple effects and help me get used to the Mathlib review process.</p>",
        "id": 614844052,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1785959984
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42534\">#42534</a> as a draft - comments are most welcome!<br>\nCurrently all proofs are either unchanged or require only superficial changes. A few lemmas are left in terms of <code>MultilinearMap (.id R) M N</code> which I plan to look at more closely to see if they can be generalized to <code>MultilinearMap σ M N</code>.</p>",
        "id": 615216154,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1786112501
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd like also to float the idea of some notation to mirror that of <code>LinearMap</code>. Perhaps something like</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>M →ₘₗ[R] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap (.id R) M N</code></li>\n<li><code>M →ₘₛₗ[σ] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap σ M N</code></li>\n<li><code>M [×n]→ₗ[R] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap (.id R) (fun i : Fin n =&gt; M) N</code></li>\n<li><code>M [×n]→ₛₗ[σ] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap σ (fun i : Fin n =&gt; M) N</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>(The latter two are in line with the notation currently in place for <code>ContinuousMultilinearMap</code>.)</p>",
        "id": 615217689,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1786112926
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why not have <code>MultisemilinearMap</code> and then make <code>MultilinearMap</code> a special case of the semilinear version?</p>",
        "id": 615220946,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1786113825
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that's not what we do for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap#doc\">docs#LinearMap</a> (which really means semilinear map)</p>",
        "id": 615221332,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786113935
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh right, I was thinking of the <code>LinearMapClass</code> and <code>SemilinearMapClass</code>, not the actual definition. My bad</p>",
        "id": 615221877,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1786114084
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just a quick status update:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42534\">#42534</a> - I am happy with its current state and reviews would be most appreciated (thanks to <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> for comments last week).</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42575\">#42575</a> - A follow-up localized to the single file <code>LinearAlgeabra/PiTensorProduct.lean</code> which generalizes <code>lift/map/map₂</code> to multi-semilinear maps.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42612\">#42612</a> - Defines the inner product on <code>PiTensorProduct</code> using the upgraded <code>PiTensorProduct.lift</code> with <code>innerₛₗ</code>. This follows very closely the construction/proofs for <code>TensorProduct</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 615993194,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1786504231
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <code>MultilinearMap</code> deserves notation as it becomes more widely used. Whatever notation we use here should mirror and be mirrored to <code>ContinuousMultilinearMap</code>. The notation set you suggested looks reasonable to me. Thanks for pushing this!</p>",
        "id": 624642798,
        "sender_full_name": "Winston Yin (尹維晨)",
        "timestamp": 1789564248
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43877\">#43877</a> adds notation</p>",
        "id": 624696688,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1789575452
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1017284\">@Gregory Loges</span> can you start a new thread about the notation?</p>",
        "id": 624697833,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1789575736
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Notation.20for.20.60MultilinearMap.60\">#mathlib4 &gt; Notation for &#96;MultilinearMap&#96;</a></p>",
        "id": 625333013,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1789762178
    }
]